# Hazard on a linear scale with periodic reference marks (every 20 mm)
# and a 60 mm electrical period. enc_fb re-latches the commutation offset
# on every index pulse while en_index is set (as src/comps/enc_fb.c does),
# and only every third mark lies at the angle conf0.mot_fb_offset was set
# for; the others commutate +-120 deg off. Moving forward, the first mark
# (+2.5 mm) is a good one, the second (+22.5 mm) is not: the axis loses
# force and runs away until the position error trips (fault 5, POS_ERROR).
# Use a single selectable reference mark, or marks every 60 mm.
@args --drive examples/linear_axis.conf --sim examples/linear_axis_sim.txt
enc_fb0.sim_ref_mode = 2
enc_fb0.sim_ref_period = 2.0944
debug_level 0
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
# probe phasing (fb_switch0.phase_mode 1) takes about 2 s on this carriage
run 2.5
lcnc 1 100
run 0.1
enc_fb0.state
fault0.fault
run 0.4
fault0.fault
@expect enc_fb0.state == 3
@expect fault0.fault[1] == 0
@expect fault0.fault == 5
